```
[+] Found factors using GCD(-5*c1 + 10*c2 + -5*c3, n)
[+] p has 1024 bits
[+] q has 1024 bits

[*] Factorization successful! Proceeding to decrypt...
[*] Decrypting modulo p...
[*] Decrypting modulo q...
[*] Combining results with CRT...

[+] FLAG: 0xL4ugh{M4t_Qu4t3rn1on_By_Zwique}
```

## Key Takeaways

- Quaternion-based cryptosystems can be vulnerable to GCD attacks when the quaternion coefficients have exploitable linear structure
- Even though matrix exponentiation is non-linear, the underlying algebraic structure can leak information about the factors
- Systematic search over small coefficient combinations can be effective for finding the right GCD relationship
